 <!-- Note: Validation is optional. Run validate-create-story for quality check before dev-story. -->
 
@@ -19,31 +19,31 @@
 
 ## Tasks / Subtasks
 
-- [ ] Add a dedicated concrete-locality layer to the canonical public board instead of relying on map narrative copy alone. (AC: 1, 2, 4)
-  - [ ] Update [DashboardScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardScreen.tsx) and the lower-grid composition so a compact nearby-stations or locality panel can sit with the existing mode field and map without breaking the Story 5.1 one-screen shell. (AC: 1, 4)
-  - [ ] Introduce or repurpose a focused component under `src/features/dashboard/components/*` for concrete locality references rather than burying all names inside the map legend. (AC: 1, 2, 4)
-  - [ ] Keep the public screen passive and board-like: no expanders, route choices, map controls, tabs, or recommendation affordances. (AC: 2, 3)
-- [ ] Extend the snapshot and presenter seam so locality references are explicit, structured, and reusable by both the board and the later map redesign. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
-  - [ ] Update [dashboard-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/contracts/dashboard-snapshot.js) with a narrow normalized structure for named nearby references, such as stations, stops, or corridors, plus any short supporting locality labels required for plain-language reading. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
-  - [ ] Update [overall-departure-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/data/overall-departure-snapshot.js) so fixture data contains concrete nearby names that reflect the Royal Institution context and no longer relies mainly on abstract corridor phrasing. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
-  - [ ] Update [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js) so the UI receives concise display-ready locality references and plain-language captions instead of generic labels like `Nearby node`. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
-- [ ] Tighten locality copy so unfamiliar viewers can name what is nearby without drifting into route advice. (AC: 1, 2, 3, 4)
-  - [ ] Replace abstract copy that makes users decode phrases like `local corridor` as the primary meaning with concrete names such as stations, stops, or named streets where they aid comprehension. (AC: 1, 2)
-  - [ ] Keep locality wording factual and descriptive only; avoid `best route`, `take`, `switch to`, `recommended`, `head for`, or similar advisory phrasing. (AC: 3)
-  - [ ] Preserve the Story 5.2 compact row grammar and Story 5.1 hierarchy so named references support the board rather than turning it back into prose. (AC: 3, 4)
-- [ ] Keep Story 5.3 clearly separated from the map-overhaul work owned by Story 5.4. (AC: 3, 4)
-  - [ ] Limit map changes to small enabling adjustments needed to keep names and locality cues coherent with the new explicit panel or field. (AC: 3, 4)
-  - [ ] Do not introduce a new map library, remote tile dependency, route drawing, or a second map implementation path. (AC: 3, 4)
